														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4864110">
									

<p>Seeking Greenlights: Yes<br />
Page Type: SCP article<br />
Genre: Slightly leaning towards horror, but not really. A bit similar to Cain/Plague doctor genre.<br />
Elevator pitch: An odd Researcher. She seems to have lived for an unnatural amount of time, possible millennia, and seems to know know everything that has happened in the past or is happening in the present, and always states that she is conducting research. She creates objects, often anomalous, for her research. These substances disappear when she has finished her research on that substance. She states that she wants to help the universe and all the universes, but refuses to divulge anything more than that on what her research<br />
Central Narrative: A sample of a previously believed impossible to create chemical substance by geological researchers in the Gobi desert. This sample was claimed by a young blind woman in a lab coat, who appeared to be able to see despite her lack of eyes. When she was denied the request, she created another sample instead. Due to this, she was reported to the SCP. When confronted, she went willingly, saying &quot;Hmm, this may help with my research. I always wanted to find more about some anomalies.&quot; She seems to know about the existence of every SCP and all secret information, despite never being informed. She creates anomalous objects to conduct often bizarre research on, seemingly out of nowhere, and has a journal which she records her findings on. This journal has many anomalous properties, but all that is written on it is basic, third-grade arithmetic. Though she is generally amiable and helpful, she refuses to divulge any information on what her research is, saying that the SCP researchers will not understand, except that it is for good. Every so often, she requests to meet another SCP, which is always denied.<br />
Hook/Attention grabber: A researcher, whom no one understands what her research is, while creating bizarre anomalies in the path of her research. Also, she knows almost everything about every SCP, which creates quite a unique threat.</p>

